 Gerais, Espírito Santo, Rio de Janeiro, and São Paulo are estimated.
 Again, considering a 2% annual growth in industrial production, Rio de
 Janeiro is the most sensitive state with 0.19 elasticity, followed by Espírito
 Santo with a 0.09 elasticity.
 Minas Gerais and São Paulo are estimated to have elasticity of 0.07 and
 0.08, respectively.
 
\end_layout

